The Birth of LangChain (Late 2022)

In October 2022, Harrison started writing a small Python library in his spare time.

Initially, it was only a few hundred lines of code on his personal GitHub account.

His goal was simple:

"Make it easier for developers to build applications using large language models."

At that time:

There was no company.
There were no investors.
It was simply an open-source hobby project.

====

Then ChatGPT Changed Everything

In November 2022, OpenAI released ChatGPT.

Millions of developers suddenly wanted to build AI applications.

A common question became:

"How do I connect ChatGPT to my own documents, databases, and APIs?"

LangChain already solved many of these problems, so it became very popular almost overnight

===

Creating the Company

As the project grew, Harrison partnered with Ankush Gola.

Together they founded the LangChain company in early 2023.

The company was established in San Francisco, California, USA.

Why is it Called "LangChain"?

The name combines:

Lang → Language Models
Chain → Chaining multiple AI operations together

Example:

User Question
      ↓
Search PDF
      ↓
Retrieve Information
      ↓
Send to GPT
      ↓
Generate Answer

This sequence is a "chain" of operations.

===

What Problems Did LangChain Solve?

Instead of developers writing everything manually, LangChain provided reusable building blocks.

| Before LangChain     | With LangChain            |
| -------------------- | ------------------------- |
| Manual prompts       | Prompt Templates          |
| Manual memory        | Memory components         |
| Manual PDF reading   | Document Loaders          |
| Manual chunking      | Text Splitters            |
| Manual embeddings    | Embedding interfaces      |
| Manual vector search | Vector Store integrations |
| Manual workflows     | Chains                    |
| Manual tool calling  | Agents and Tools          |


