====

s LangChain Free?

Yes.

The core LangChain framework is open source and free to use.

The company also offers commercial products such as LangSmith for organisations that need advanced testing and observability.

Why Did LangChain Become So Popular?

It became popular because it reduced the amount of code developers needed to write.

Instead of implementing everything from scratch, developers could quickly assemble AI applications using ready-made components.

Your Bus Booking Chatbot vs. LangChain

Your chatbot works without LangChain because you already wrote the orchestration logic yourself.

For example, your project has:

Conversation Manager
Bus Search Agent
Seat Selection Agent
Booking Agent
Payment Agent
Confirmation Agent

These components coordinate the workflow directly. LangChain simply provides a framework that can help developers build similar workflows 
more quickly—it isn't required if you already have a well-designed architecture.

